---
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/ui/PageHeader.astro";
import { analyticsSettings, EVENTS, MAX_ERRORS_PER_PAGE } from "../config/analytics";
import { pageTitle, site } from "../config/site";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

// What this page says about analytics comes from the same settings that decide whether the pages
// carry the tracker, so a build without analytics cannot claim them and one with them cannot
// hide them (ADR 0051).
const analytics = analyticsSettings();
const description = analytics
  ? "What NetworksInsights does with your data: no accounts, no cookies, visit statistics without personal data, and one theme setting kept on your device."
  : "What NetworksInsights does with your data today: no accounts, no cookies, no analytics, and one theme preference stored on your device.";

// The one list of crumbs, drawn on the page and written into its structured data (ADR 0039).
const breadcrumbs = [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy" }];
---

<Page breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} title={pageTitle("Privacy")} description={description}>
  <div class="grid gap-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    <PageHeader
      title="Privacy"
      intro={`This page describes what ${site.name} does with your data today. It is short because the site does very little.`}
    />
  </div>

  <div class="ni-prose">
    <h2>In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>There are no accounts and no sign-up.</li>
      <li>The site sets no cookies.</li>
      {analytics ? (
  <li>
    The site counts visits, tool use and errors with Umami, without cookies and without storing your
    IP address. It has no advertising trackers.
  </li>
) : (
  <li>The site has no analytics and no advertising trackers today.</li>
)}
      <li>Your theme choice is stored on your own device and never sent to us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name}{" "}
      is a set of static pages. Loading a page does not ask you for information, and the site has no
      forms that send data to us. The fonts are served from the site itself, so your browser does
      not contact a font service either.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The site sets no cookies. It stores one item in your browser's local storage, under the key
      <code>ni-theme</code>: your choice of light, dark or system theme, if you make one. It stays
      on your device, and the site does not read it for any other purpose.
    </p>
    <p>
      So that tools keep working without a connection, the site's service worker keeps a copy of the
      site's own pages you open, and of the code they need, in your browser's cache: up to the last
      hundred pages. It never keeps what you type or the files you open in a tool, and it never
      sends anything anywhere. Clearing your browser's data for this site removes the copies.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    {analytics ? (
  <Fragment>
    <p>
      To learn which tools people use, which pages are slow and what breaks, the site uses
      <a href="https://umami.is/">Umami Cloud</a>, a cookie-free analytics service. Its script is
      served from this site; what it measures is sent to Umami. It sets no cookies and cannot follow
      you to other sites.
    </p>
    <p>For each page you open, it sends:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        the page address, without anything after a <code>?</code> or <code>#</code>
      </li>
      <li>the page title, and the address of the site that linked you here, if any</li>
      <li>your screen size and your browser's language</li>
      <li>
        how fast the page loaded and responded (Core Web Vitals: LCP, INP, CLS, and two related
        timings).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      On a tool page it also sends one "{EVENTS.toolUsed}" event the first time you use the tool,
      with the tool's name and nothing you entered. If the page hits a programming error, it sends
      at most {MAX_ERRORS_PER_PAGE} "{EVENTS.error}" reports: the kind of error, its message with
      any quoted text, web addresses, email addresses and long numbers removed, and the file and
      line of our code where it happened.
    </p>
    <p>
      Umami receives your IP address with each request, as any server does, and does not store it.
      It uses it to estimate your country and region, and to count visitors: it combines your IP
      address and browser with a secret value that changes every month, so repeat visits within a
      month count as one visitor and nothing links you from one month to the next. See
      <a href="https://umami.is/privacy">Umami's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing is sent if your browser sends Do Not Track, or if a content blocker stops the script.
      The script reads one local storage key, <code>umami.disabled</code>, which lets the site's
      owner leave their own visits out of the numbers. It never writes anything to your browser.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
) : (
  <p>
    There are no analytics today. If that changes, this page will be updated before analytics go
    live.
  </p>
)}

    <h2>Tools and your files</h2>
    <p>
      Every tool page says where that tool does its work. The site has no tool that sends your files
      or text to a server: they are processed in your browser, on your device, and are never sent to
      us or to the analytics service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some tools need a larger file to do their job: a PDF engine, an image decoder, an audio
      encoder, a text-recognition language file or an AI model (used by Background Remover, Image
      Upscaler and Speech to Text). Your browser downloads that file from this site, and may keep it
      for later. It is a download only: nothing you enter goes with it. Once downloaded, the tool
      works on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare. To deliver a page, Cloudflare necessarily receives technical
      request data, such as your IP address and the page you asked for. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>
      for how it handles that data.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name}{" "}
      is run by Wasey Jamal, an individual in India. It is not a registered company. For any
      question about this page or about your data, write to
      <a href="mailto:contact@networksinsights.com">contact@networksinsights.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>This page is governed by the laws of India.</p>
  </div>
</Page>
